Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 19:00:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] pl022: start a burst with the queued frame and stop it
 without a stray clock edge

A write to SSPDR on an idle controller started the clocking thread with
transmitData still zero, so the first frame on the wire was 0x00 and the
byte the driver wrote followed it; the thread took the queued frame only
when the first frame's bit counter wrapped. At the end of a burst the stop
branch of Step() drove SCK and TX low and then fell through into the clock
toggle, raising SCK once more with the thread already stopped. A slave that
samples on the rising edge saw a ghost frame start and a spurious bit before
every burst. The first frame is now dequeued at the write that starts the
thread, and Step() returns after stopping, so SCK idles low between bursts
as SPI mode 0 requires and the wire carries exactly the frames written.
---
 emulation/peripherals/spi/rp2040_spi.cs | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/emulation/peripherals/spi/rp2040_spi.cs b/emulation/peripherals/spi/rp2040_spi.cs
--- a/emulation/peripherals/spi/rp2040_spi.cs
+++ b/emulation/peripherals/spi/rp2040_spi.cs
@@ -243,6 +243,7 @@
           SetMultiplePins(clockPins, false);
           _executionThread.Stop();
           running = false;
+          return;
         }
       }
 
@@ -366,6 +367,9 @@
             txBuffer.Enqueue((ushort)value);
             if (!running)
             {
+              txBuffer.TryDequeue(out transmitData);
+              transmitCounter = 0;
+              receiveData = 0;
               running = true;
               _executionThread.Start();
             }
